NotesAI-RNA Application - Feature Guide
======================================

This document lists the major features in NotesAI-RNA and describes what they do.

1) Authentication and Account
- Register, login, and logout with username, email, and password.
- JWT access + refresh flow with automatic refresh on 401 (retry once).
- Tokens stored in localStorage and cookies for session continuity.
- Password reset flow (request + confirm with uid/token).
- In-account password change.
- Account deletion with confirmation.
- Profile endpoint used to show current user info.

2) AI API Key and Model Selection
- Optional OpenRouter API key stored on the server (encrypted).
- Device PIN required to unlock the API key form; PIN can be set and changed.
- Toggle between using the server key or your own key.
- Model selection dropdown in AI Chat and Notes AI actions.

3) Notes Management (Rich Editor)
- Create, edit, and delete notes with title, subject, category, tags, and content.
- Rich editor toolbar: bold, italic, underline, bulleted list, numbered list, headings, font selection, and clear formatting.
- Search and filter notes by text and subject.
- Reader view shows tags, metadata (updated time, editor), and full note content.

4) Notes AI Actions
- AI actions on a note: summarize, explain, and generate questions.
- Responses display inside the note reader panel.
- AI interactions are stored in local AI history.

5) Tasks Management
- Create, edit, and delete tasks.
- Priority levels and due dates.
- Mark tasks complete or active.
- Filter tasks by active/completed.
- Task lists are ordered with incomplete items first and then by due date.

6) AI Chat (NotesAI-RNA AI)
- Multi-session chat workspace with saved history per user.
- Filters: General, Deep Research, and Writing.
- Deep Research is used for more structured analysis and longer-form reasoning.
- Writing is used for drafting, rewriting, and polishing content.
- Session history can be renamed and deleted.
- Image-to-text import (OCR) inserts extracted text into the chat input.

7) Sharing and Collaboration
- Share links for notes, tasks, and chat sessions.
- Permissions: read (view only) or collab (collaborate with other users).
- Invite users to a share, list members, remove members, and revoke links.
- Share management panel to copy links and manage members.
- Shared access screen supports token-based viewing and collaboration.
- Invited users can accept or decline from the shared access screen.

8) Notifications
- Notification center and notifications page with unread count.
- Mark one or all notifications as read; clear all.
- Automated notifications:
  - Share invites and share activity.
  - Task due and due-soon alerts.
  - Periodic study reminders.
- Optional browser notifications when permission is granted.

9) Offline-First Sync
- Notes, tasks, and AI history are stored in IndexedDB for offline use.
- Local changes are saved immediately and marked as pending.
- Sync runs on app start, auth changes, online events, and periodic intervals.
- Pending actions (create/update/delete) are merged with server data once online.

10) Navigation and UI
- Single-page app with views: Home, Notes, Tasks, NotesAI-RNA AI, Shares, Notifications, Account.
- Responsive left sidebar navigation with a mobile overlay.
- Theme toggle (light/dark) with persisted preference.
- Cookie consent banner for core app functionality.

11) Platform and API Modules
- Frontend: React + Vite (PWA assets included).
- Backend: Django + Django REST Framework + SimpleJWT.
- OCR: Tesseract.js for image-to-text in AI chat.
- Primary API namespaces:
  - /api/auth/
  - /api/notes/
  - /api/tasks/
  - /api/ai/
  - /api/share/
  - /api/notifications/

Notes
- OpenRouter is the AI provider. You can use the server key or your own key in Account Settings.
